            <ArticleTitle>Unicameral Bone Cyst of the Medial Cuneiform.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>357-360</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A unicameral bone cyst is a relatively uncommon, benign bone tumor found in the metaphysis of long bones, such as the humerus and the femur, in skeletally immature persons. In the foot, these benign, fluid-filled cavities are most commonly found within the os calcis. We present a case report of a 10-year-old female with a unicameral bone cyst of the medial cuneiform.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
